Hello all,

I need some help with longitudinal measurements. I am trying to model latent trait of individuals using items, designed to measure the same trait but completely different items, at different moments. I am considering three different types of models as you can see in the attached figure. I would like to simultaneously estimate item and individual parameters and make sure that all are in the same scale. Measurements will be done months apart. Hopefully, I would like NOT to use common itens in the measurements.Is this possible?

My understanding is that

With Model 1, the scale of the items in moments 1 and 2 will be different. Is this correct?

With Model 2, the scale of the items in moments 1 and 2 will be the same. Is this correct?

With Model 3, the scale of the items in moments 1 and 2 will be the same. The assumption here is that the items will be equated with the linking test. Is this correct? If yes, how can  I pass these info to MIRT?

Any insight or references will help me greatly and will be highly welcome!

Looking forward to hearing from you,

Hugo

